{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"014982e31e60bef21033d2c03246360413d7905f96d5ee8673b25149aa3f110e","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_09514c3729c19d4197b81ea20476f8197ea6c01659fc0261fd9cd4cdc8f36660","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical contribution to machine comprehension but fails to meet key policy and compliance standards. The most significant issue is the violation of double-blind review policies due to the explicit inclusion of author names, affiliations, and email addresses. Additionally, the paper lacks a broader impact statement and ethical considerations, which are increasingly important in AI research. While the data usage is compliant with standard licensing terms, the absence of these policy-related elements weakens the submission's adherence to conference guidelines and responsible research practices.","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","paper_identity_sha256":"f0a3523c05db60e2bbdf762391461d827fcf15b4fadeee965368011497aa49c4","prompt_identity_sha256":"9490323614c090ec7ff17748b00e9af9ef31814237fc72e1fc5be2b832c2f521","raw_response_sha256":"34c7ca20ca59939b81f40c80f0b34d0bc369a0add6488f277e18f8b7f2e16143","request_identity_sha256":"cd2b79595b16aabb5be34d3ace0e178930e829420b9698d6554da31c05395294","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms associated with the deployment of machine comprehension systems. While the task of question answering is generally benign, the lack of discussion on potential biases in the SQuAD dataset (which is derived from Wikipedia) or the societal impact of automated reading comprehension is a notable omission. The authors do not address issues of fairness across different demographic groups or the potential for the model to propagate biases present in the source text. Given the 2017 context, a broader impact statement was not yet a strict requirement for all ICLR submissions, but its absence limits the paper's compliance with modern responsible AI standards.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the Stanford Question Answering Dataset (SQuAD) v1.1, which is a publicly available benchmark dataset. The authors correctly cite the source of the data (Rajpurkar et al., 2016) and acknowledge that the passages are derived from Wikipedia articles. The use of Wikipedia content is consistent with the Creative Commons licensing typically associated with Wikipedia, and the SQuAD dataset itself is distributed for research purposes. There is no indication of privacy violations, as the data consists of public news articles and encyclopedic entries rather than personally identifiable information (PII) from private individuals. The use of GloVe word embeddings is also standard and compliant with their respective licensing terms.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The submission violates double-blind review policies. The title page explicitly lists the authors' names (Shuohang Wang and Jing Jiang) and their institutional affiliation (School of Information Systems, Singapore Management University). Additionally, the authors' email addresses are provided on the first page. These details clearly identify the authors and their institution, which is prohibited in double-blind review processes to prevent bias. The acknowledgments section also thanks specific individuals (Pranav Rajpurkar and Percy Liang), which, while common, further reduces anonymity, though the primary violation is the explicit author identification on the title page.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-038"],"review_text":"There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission in the provided text. The authors properly cite prior work, including their own previous work on match-LSTM (Wang & Jiang, 2016) and the Pointer Net model (Vinyals et al., 2015). The methodology is presented as a novel combination of these existing components applied to the SQuAD dataset. The references are comprehensive and appear to be correctly formatted. No textual overlap with other known publications is evident from the provided markdown, and the content appears to be original to this submission.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper lacks a comprehensive broader impact statement. While the conclusion mentions future work, it does not discuss the societal implications of the technology, such as its potential use in educational tools, information retrieval, or the risks of automated misinformation detection. There is no mention of software or code licensing, nor is there a statement regarding the availability of the code for reproducibility. The paper does not include any required checklists or ethics approvals, which were not standard for ICLR 2017 but are relevant for assessing current compliance. The absence of these elements limits the transparency and accountability of the research.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5183659c7fc12bf476d1270caf8ecf33f154fbdc44c2aef2dea1c0096184adb6","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","paper_ordinal":1,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"34c7ca20ca59939b81f40c80f0b34d0bc369a0add6488f277e18f8b7f2e16143","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"2a7f41b60e2118d9f2e0f8d4554570bfed745db6dc3c912c1f347f12f05c4a2c","request_identity_sha256":"cd2b79595b16aabb5be34d3ace0e178930e829420b9698d6554da31c05395294","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":1021,"prompt_tokens":18691,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19712},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"cd2b79595b16aabb5be34d3ace0e178930e829420b9698d6554da31c05395294","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}